Inference image: install with uv, as the project beside it does

Upstream migrated apps/inference to uv at 643e5bb (PEP 621 project
table, [tool.uv.sources], uv.lock; poetry.lock deleted; Makefile, README
and CI on `uv sync`), but left apps/inference/Dockerfile on
`pip install poetry` and `poetry install --only main`. Poetry does not
read [tool.uv.sources], so chatspace (editable, vendor/chatspace),
steerllm (vendor/chatspace/steerllm), transformer-lens (git fork) and
neuronpedia-inference-client (path) resolve to nothing, and every cuda
build at pin e5488b2a fails with "neuronpedia-inference depends on
chatspace (*) which doesn't match any versions" once the interpreter
problem (KB-76, patch 0002) is out of the way. The Dockerfile also
copied only pyproject.toml and poetry.lock* before installing, so
vendor/ was absent at install time regardless (KB-77).

This replaces the poetry block of the final stage with a pinned uv,
copies uv.lock and vendor/ beside the project file, and runs
`uv sync --frozen --no-dev` against the image's interpreter. The venv
is placed at /opt/venv and put first on PATH, because upstream's
compose.inference.dev.yaml bind mounts apps/inference over the image's
copy, which would hide a venv inside it; CMD and the dev overlay's
`python start.py` are unchanged. base-nocuda (python:3.10-slim) is not
touched and remains unbuildable for the KB-76 reason; this repository
builds only the cuda stage.

Upstream tracking: not yet filed. No upstream fix exists to bump to:
the next commit touching this file, 17bc391, deletes every Dockerfile
and compose file in the upstream repository, so a pin bump past it is a
deployment change rather than a version bump. Delete this patch at that
bump.

diff --git a/apps/inference/Dockerfile b/apps/inference/Dockerfile
index 1cfe4aa..f863d9e 100644
--- a/apps/inference/Dockerfile
+++ b/apps/inference/Dockerfile
@@ -106,28 +106,33 @@ RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
     ca-certificates \
     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
 
-# Install poetry
-RUN pip install poetry
-
-ENV POETRY_VIRTUALENVS_CREATE=false
-RUN poetry config virtualenvs.create false
-
-# Configure poetry/pip to use custom CA if provided
+# The project moved to uv (pyproject [tool.uv.sources], uv.lock); poetry cannot resolve
+# its path and git sources. Pinned; bump deliberately.
+RUN pip install uv==0.9.30
+
+# The venv lives outside /app/apps/inference because compose.inference.dev.yaml bind
+# mounts that directory over the image's copy at runtime. PATH keeps the CMD below and
+# the dev overlay's `python start.py` on the venv interpreter.
+ENV UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/opt/venv \
+    UV_PYTHON_DOWNLOADS=never \
+    UV_LINK_MODE=copy \
+    PATH=/opt/venv/bin:$PATH
+
+# Configure pip to use custom CA if provided
 RUN if [ -n "${CUSTOM_CA_BUNDLE}" ] && [ "${CUSTOM_CA_BUNDLE}" != ".nocustomca" ]; then \
-    pip config set global.cert /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt && \
-    poetry config certificates.default.cert /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt; \
+    pip config set global.cert /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt; \
     fi
 
 # Copy the client package first
 COPY packages/python/neuronpedia-inference-client /app/packages/python/neuronpedia-inference-client/
 
-# Copy only poetry files
-COPY apps/inference/pyproject.toml apps/inference/poetry.lock* apps/inference/
+# Lock, project file and the vendored path sources the lock points at
+COPY apps/inference/pyproject.toml apps/inference/uv.lock apps/inference/
+COPY apps/inference/vendor apps/inference/vendor/
 WORKDIR /app/apps/inference
 
-# Install only main dependencies
-ENV POETRY_REQUESTS_TIMEOUT=30
-RUN poetry install --only main
+# Exactly the lock, main dependencies only; the project itself is not a package
+RUN uv sync --frozen --no-dev --python /usr/bin/python
 
 # Now copy the rest of the application code
 COPY apps/inference /app/apps/inference/
